  "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#semiotic_projection_1",
  "@type": "SemioticProjection",
  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the child as the subject of the text",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the child (visual material) because the text 'mom won't let me use the oven with my friends' uses the first-person pronoun 'me', which directly refers to the child depicted in the image. The child is the central subject of the meme, and the text explicitly identifies her as 'me', creating a direct semiotic projection where the viewer sees themselves as the child in the scenario. This projection is reinforced by the child's joyful expression, which the user may relate to as their own experience or perspective.",
